  "sampleStartName": "Getting started.md",
  "sampleExportName": "Export guide.md",
  "sampleDesign": "# Theme design notes\n\nWrite, read and organize the same Markdown document. Keep your place when switching views.\n\n## Design principles\n\n### Stay immersed\n\nKeep the focus on your words. Show essential tools while writing and give the document more space when reading or arranging its structure.\n\n### Reduce visual noise\n\nUse hierarchy, spacing and a few accent colors to express relationships. Borders, buttons and status messages should stay quiet.\n\n## Theme colors\n\nThemes need to work in both light and dark modes. Use accents for selection, navigation and primary actions, with consistent contrast for body text.\n\n- Choose light and dark modes independently\n- Eight palettes share semantic tokens\n\n## Typography and spacing\n\nPrioritize comfortable reading and clear headings. Map summaries show the first thirty characters by default; select a node to read its full section.\n\n## Consistent exports\n\n> The same content should keep a clear structure in the editor, the reading view and exported files.\n\n| Format | Use |\n| --- | --- |\n| HTML | Publishing online |\n| PDF | Reading and sharing |\n\n```markdown\n# This is code, not a heading node\n```",
  "sampleWeekly": "# Weekly review\n\n## This week\n\n- [x] Confirm the three main views\n- [ ] Collect feedback from real use\n\n## Next week\n\nMake structural thinking part of everyday Markdown writing.",
  "sampleReading": "# Reading notes\n\n## Writing is thinking\n\nWriting helps you see the missing links in an idea.\n\n> Good tools make ideas clearer.\n\n## From notes to an article\n\n### Collect material\n\nKeep the original material and its sources.\n\n### Organize the structure\n\nGroup related ideas. Set the hierarchy first, then add supporting evidence.",
  "sampleStart": "# Getting started\n\n## Edit\n\nClick the document to edit it, or switch to source. All views share the same content and undo history.\n\n## Read\n\nEight palettes and six typography styles are saved independently of the content.\n\n## Map\n\nDouble-click a node to edit a section. Long-press and drag it onto another section to change its parent.\n\n## Local files\n\nOpen your Markdown from the File menu. Save with Ctrl+S. Unsaved changes are kept as recovery drafts.",
  "sampleExport": "# Export guide\n\n## Markdown\n\nSave as standard UTF-8 text to continue in other editors.\n\n## HTML\n\nExport a standalone page with the current typography and colors.\n\n## PDF and Word\n\nExport documents for reading and sharing.\n\n## Map image\n\nExport the complete tree structure as PNG.",
  "guideDocument": "# Welcome to Vex\n\nClick the document and write your first idea.\n\n## From content to structure\n\nArrange sections in the map and the text follows.\n\n## Share your work\n\nChoose a style and export your document.",
